 The ad should be in the form of a letter from the owner to their customers, and it's written in a casual, conversational tone with some humor.
Subject: Haircut Heaven is Here! (And It’s 25% Off!)

Dear Valued Customers,

I hope this message finds you well, and your hair hasn’t been growing out of control like mine has lately. I know what you’re thinking—“Why would anyone need a haircut?!” But let me explain. My hair has grown so long that I can now use it as a curtain to hide my face when I’m being photographed by my cat, Mr. Whiskers. He thinks he’s a professional photographer.

Anyway, I’ve decided to throw a little party at Haircut Heaven, and guess what? You’re invited! We’re offering a 25% discount on all our services because, honestly, I think we’ve been charging too much for such great haircuts. Plus, I’ve realized that even though I charge a lot, my hair still looks terrible. So, it’s time to give back to the community—and also to make sure my wallet doesn’t get any more damaged than it already is.

So, whether you want a classic fade, a trendy buzz cut, or something completely wild and unpredictable (we have a special section for that), we’ve got you covered. Our stylists are not only skilled but also very good at making you feel comfortable, even if you’re the type of person who always says “no” to anything involving hair.

But wait—there’s more! If you bring a friend, they’ll get an extra 10% off. That means you can both get your hair done and then go out and do something fun together, like arguing about which hairstyle is better. Or maybe just sitting quietly in a chair while someone else does your hair. Either way, it’s a win-win.

Don’t miss out on this opportunity to look fabulous and save money. Remember, life is too short for bad haircuts, and your bank account is too sensitive for expensive ones. Come in, relax, and let us transform your locks into something worthy of a magazine cover—or at least a Instagram post that doesn’t make you cringe.

See you soon!

Warm regards,
[Your Name]
Owner, Haircut Heaven

P.S. If you’re feeling particularly adventurous, ask for the “Surprise Cut.” No refunds, no guarantees, and no apologies. Just a new look, and possibly a few surprises. (We promise it’s not a surprise in the sense of a prank, but more like a creative twist.)

